Z||000000||JamesWM83||08-26-2001||10:30 PM||||What can I do? I Have some good ???'s<BR>Here we go:<BR>1) what are the BEST plugs/wires for out cars?<BR>2) what are some cool bolt on's for performance?<BR>3) my car has slow pick up... what can I do to it to get it back up?<BR>4) clutch is really loose... and it's really hard to shift.. what can I do to fix that?<P>Any help with any of these ??'s would be greatly appreciated. Thank you!<P>------------------<BR>~James<P>1986 Fiero GT! <BR>2.8 4 clicker. White face guages, blue backlighting, grey marlbe dash kit, IRM sie rocker scoops, fierostore.com 1/4 window scoop, V8 Archie Warber hood, rear added sway bar, silver mesh inserts in tail-lights, mesh inserts in turn lamp and grill, KYB shocks and struts, Eibach lowering springs, 300 watt amp, and 600 watt 12" sub, clarion pro audio 5x6" plates, Kenwood Xcelon 4x10's, clarion pro audio cd player, monster calbe wiring, rockford wiring, pheonix gold wiring, chrome ocelot exhaust tips||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||08-27-2001||08:45 AM||||... wires.. uum NEW ones.. bosch, taylor, MSD, Mallory. anything is better then old.. well not Vitek but Nology and what not are ok. uum i'm very happy with my NGK -ur5- plugs in my nitrous fed V6. as for the best bolt ons.. uum have a 2.5" exhaust made it'll be about $350, the obvious K&N Drop in filter part number e-0890. uuum take the throttle body off and clean it along with the intake pelenum.. odds are it's all nasty and full of carbon depostis from the EGR. get an MSD 6a box and Crane PS91 coil. then a Nitrous Express wet system. you'll have a 13 second monster for under $1000. as for the clutch. <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A>  they have a Kush-lok get that and a NEW pressure plate from NAPA. and have it installed. that it'll be another $650 or so. (10 hours at $65 p/h) or find a local fiero nut and give him $400 to change the clutch. <BR> <BR>the clutch i had in my 86 SE... held over 300lbft at the wheels.. would chirp 4th at 80+<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst4puck.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kasdan||08-27-2001||09:01 AM||||I use the Bosch Platinum plugs, magnacore wires, Conrad Distribuiter cap, thats good as far as ignition.  Bolt ons....turbo, NOS, bigger throddle body, headers, aluminium heads, aluminum block, etc.  Dont know much of a clutch, my GT is an auto.<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan<BR>1986 GT Fastback, <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FIERO2.JPG">       <BR>Holley Ram-Air, Power Steering, K&N Filtercharger, Bosch Wires, Bosch Platinum Plugs, Conrad Distribuiter Cap/Rotor, New GT Seats, New Headliner, New Carpet, Ocelet Exhaust, Red Underbody Light Kit (coming soon)<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula88||08-27-2001||09:06 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>... wires.. uum NEW ones.. bosch, taylor, MSD, Mallory. anything is better then old.. well not Vitek but Nology and what not are ok. uum i'm very happy with my NGK -ur5- plugs in my nitrous fed V6. as for the best bolt ons.. uum have a 2.5" exhaust made it'll be about $350, the obvious K&N Drop in filter part number e-0890. uuum take the throttle body off and clean it along with the intake pelenum.. odds are it's all nasty and full of carbon depostis from the EGR. get an MSD 6a box and Crane PS91 coil. then a Nitrous Express wet system. you'll have a 13 second monster for under $1000. as for the clutch. <A HREF="http://www.clutchnet.com" TARGET=_blank>www.clutchnet.com</A>  they have a Kush-lok get that and a NEW pressure plate from NAPA. and have it installed. that it'll be another $650 or so. (10 hours at $65 p/h) or find a local fiero nut and give him $400 to change the clutch. <BR> <BR>the clutch i had in my 86 SE... held over 300lbft at the wheels.. would chirp 4th at 80+<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst4puck.jpg">  <P>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-27-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So, how was that 4-puck for driveability?  How about wear and tear on the flywheel?  I've got a Ram in my Formula now, but it'll need a stronger clutch if I do any mods.  Nitrous would blow that clutch away pretty fast, I imagine.  Are you recommending a stock replacement pressure plate or a stronger one?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000004||Fiero_24||08-27-2001||09:17 AM||||Check out my site for what I am doing to my 2.8.  1FST2M6, I am building this motor to take a good shot from a 6 fogger setup like  the one I talked to you before about.  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24/V6project.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24/V6project.html</A> <P>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000005||1FST2M6||08-27-2001||02:41 PM||||it SUCKED in traffic but i had a 2600# pressure plate.. i put the same disc in a friends 86 GT with a stock pressure plate and it was much better. the dash didnt' shake and you could still chirp 3rd pretty good. the Kush-lok unit is better.. had virtualy no chatter and will be nicer to the flywheel. the 4 puck WILL destroy your flywheel.. but it takes a long time and the $200 sacrifice of the flywheel was/is well worth the tire lifting ability of the cermaic pads and better pressure plate. <P>thats quite a shopping list you've got. does the car run at all now? if it does go have it dynoed for a true before and after... and get a hold of <A HREF="http://www.nitrouswarehouse.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nitrouswarehouse.com</A>  for your nitrous parts. the Nitrous Express stuff he sells is WAY better than the NOS stuff i've had. I'm MUCH happier with NX. better solenoids, nicer filter. and STUPID more HP! with nearly the same jetting as my dry system. for a true 6 fogger system you'll need LOTS of patience and a little luck... you'll got through quite a few feed tubes before you get the bending down pat. sure looks killer and functions just as well as it looks.. but i'm lazy and just went with the single fogger. runs good air/fuel and SMOKES my 18s   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 08-27-2001).]||||reg||1
